# Formatting and verification

## Black

- Format all Python with **Black**, `line-length = 250`.
- After editing Python, run Black on touched files (or the package) before finishing.
- Do not hand-reflow to a shorter width; Black is the source of truth.

## Verify after every code change

Before considering a coding task done, run all of:

1. `uv run black orion tests` (or the files you changed)
2. `uv run ruff check orion tests` — fix all findings
3. `uv run pyright` — Pylance uses Pyright; fix all reported type errors/warnings
4. `uv run pytest tests/core tests/ui -q` when behaviour might be affected

Do not leave the tree with Black diffs, Ruff findings, Pyright/Pylance diagnostics, or failing tests.
